 "lesson": [
  {
   "genre": "blues",
   "text": "Class, before we rock, we pay respect. Everything starts in the Mississippi Delta with the blues."
  },
  {
   "genre": "rnb",
   "text": "Speed it up, add a backbeat and a horn section, and move it to the city. Now it's rhythm and blues, and people are dancing."
  },
  {
   "genre": "rockabilly",
   "text": "Country crashes the party. A kid named Elvis walks into Sun Studio in Memphis and suddenly there's a name for this: rock and roll."
  },
  {
   "genre": "brit",
   "text": "Meanwhile, across the ocean, British kids were listening to every record. They sent it right back, louder. Beatlemania, 1964."
  },
  {
   "genre": "hardrock",
   "text": "Then Cream and Zeppelin plugged into bigger amps. That's the lesson. Pop quiz tomorrow: follow any arrow and see where it takes you."
  }
